    ("Siellä on neiti nukkununna,", "Siellä on neiti nukkunut,", "siellä, neiti, nukkua", "there, maiden, to sleep", "There a maiden has fallen asleep,", "A sleeping enchanted maiden draped in gold and silver, lying amid magical honey-grass in a hidden roofless cabin, is a classic fairy-tale image of an enclosed, otherworldly source of power guarded by sleep and secrecy — the bee must cross nine and a half seas to reach this liminal, dreamlike realm, the same supernatural distance Lemminkäinen's mother once crossed to find healing substances near the moon and sun, linking this magical-source motif across multiple episodes of the epic."),
