    ("Jo otti olut hapata,", "Jo otti olut hapata,", "jo, ottaa, olut, hapata", "now, to take/begin, beer, to ferment", "Now the beer began to ferment,", "Third time succeeds where the first two failed — the simple rule-of-three pattern resolves, and the modest, otherworldly sweetness of mead and honey (rather than violent foam or an inert pinecone) proves to be the magic ingredient, a gentle thematic resolution: true transformation comes from delicate natural sweetness rather than force."),
